Let \(\pi^*\in\arg\min_{
\pi}J_0(
\pi)\), and let \(\pi^*_{t:}\) denote its continuation after a reachable history \(h_t\). Reoptimization at \(h_t\) is time-consistent precisely when \[\pi^*_{t:}
\in\arg\min_{
\gamma}J_t(
\gamma\mid h_t),\] where \(\gamma\) ranges over feasible continuations. Time-inconsistent reoptimization occurs if this inclusion fails for at least one reachable \(h_t\): the decision maker then replaces the precommitted continuation by a conditionally preferred one. The failure concerns preference compatibility across dates, even when forecasts, feasible sets, and observations agree with the original model.
